course: dictionary
lesson: 6925
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. This is the context, and it gives you clues. «She tore open the packet and poured out the crisps.» You tear open a bag, so here a packet is a small bag or box.
explain: «The parcel came in a small packet through the letterbox.» Now packet means a small parcel sent by post. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «That new bike must have cost a packet!» Here packet does not mean a bag at all. In the UK, cost a packet is an informal way of saying something cost a lot of money. Look at the whole phrase, not just one word.
fact: A packet is a small bag or box that holds things, like seeds or crisps.
fact: A packet can also mean a small parcel sent by post.
fact: «Cost a packet» (UK, informal) means cost a lot of money.
fact: In maths, packets are groups: if each packet holds 6 pens, then 4 packets hold 24 pens.
exercise: «She tore open the packet and poured out the crisps.» In this sentence, what is a packet? | A kind of bike | A loud noise | *A small bag or box that holds things | A small parcel sent by post
exercise: «That new bike must have cost a packet!» What does cost a packet mean? | It cost very little | It was sent by post | It was a bag of seeds | *It cost a lot of money
exercise: Sam needs 20 pens. Each packet holds 6 pens. How many packets must he buy? | 20 | 6 | *4 | 3
test: «The parcel came in a small packet through the letterbox.» What does packet mean here? | *A small parcel sent by post | A seed box | A crisp bag | A sock
test: «Seed packets tell you how deep and how far apart to plant.» What do seed packets tell you? | Who sold the seeds | What colour the flowers will be | *How deep and how far apart to plant | How many seeds are in the sky
exam: Which sentence uses packet to mean a small parcel sent by post? | The shop sells seeds in a tiny box | *A small parcel arrived for me in the post today | I ate a packet of crisps after school | We counted the pens in the packet
